ame and type', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'Iterator returns RRsets in lexical order of names, and for identical names in ascending order of type numeric value (e.g., A (1) before AAAA (28)). For a zone containing RRsets: A record for b.example.com, AAAA record for a.example.com, MX record for a.example.com, the iterator yields: AAAA(a.example.com), MX(a.example.com), A(b.example.com).', 'description': 'Verify that ZoneIterator sorts RRsets first by the fully‑qualified name (lexicographically) and then by the DNS type code, ensuring deterministic AXFR ordering.'}, {'input': [], 'expected': 'When two RRsets share the same name but different types (e.g., A and AAAA for www.example.com), the iterator yields the lower type number first (A before AAAA).', 'description': 'Confirm that for identical names the iterator respects type ordering rather than insertion order.'}]}, {'group': 'AXFR iterator throws ConcurrentModificationException after zone modification', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'ConcurrentModificationException thrown when calling next() on the iterator after adding a new RRset to the Zone.', 'description': 'Obtain an iterator via zone.AXFR(), then add an additional RRset to the same Zone before invoking iterator.next(). The iterator should detect the structural change and raise ConcurrentModificationException.'}]}, {'group': 'AXFR iterator throws NullPointerException when a null RRset is present', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NullPointerException thrown during iteration when the Zone contains a null RRset entry.', 'description': "Directly insert a null RRset into the Zone's internal storage (e.g., via reflection or a specially crafted addRRset(null) if the method permits null). Calling zone.AXFR() and then iterator.next() should encounter the null entry and raise NullPointerException."}]}, {'group': 'AXFR iterator throws IllegalStateException after iterator is exhausted and next() called again', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'Illeg